{"id":150360457,"slug":"i-wish-i-was-a-little-bit-taller","title":"I Wish I Was A Little Bit Taller - Antidepressants and Reduced Height in Kids","subtitle":"What we don't know might be making us less likely to be a baller","post_date":"2024-10-17T17:46:31.662Z","audience":"everyone","type":"newsletter","canonical_url":"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/i-wish-i-was-a-little-bit-taller","wordcount":408,"source":"api","fetched_at":"2026-09-13T21:51:00.341Z","body_sha256":"3d8eac25b503909357ddb4e864943b1b0ad7a07799b1952db5017e8e6e60a3fa","text_words":470,"complete":true,"body_html":"<p><strong>The Frontier Psychiatrists</strong> is reporting live from AACAP 2024!  This article is very <em>on brand</em> given my book, <a href=\"https://amzn.to/3RXn03G\">Inessential Pharmacology.</a> (amazon link)</p><p>Do antidepressants have adverse effects in kids your author didn't know about yet?  As it turns out…yes.   It is ironic, given my “<a href=\"https://open.substack.com/pub/thefrontierpsychiatrists/p/the-muir-skee-lo-emotionally-corrective?r=1ct8f&amp;utm_campaign=post&amp;utm_medium=web\">Muir-Skee Lo Emotionally Corrective Equation</a>” argument…which, to be concise, is that height difference is an excellent way to explain “size of difference?”</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!tZf_!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6b08e42b-c3b6-4458-9a4a-816886646cd0_4032x3024.jpeg\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!tZf_!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F6b08e42b-c3b6-4458-9a4a-816886646cd0_4032x3024.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!tZf_!,w_848,